# This repository *is* the contents of the CIRCUITPY drive, so it lives on a
# removable FAT volume that macOS, Windows and Linux all scribble on.  None
# of that belongs in git: tracking it means every `git pull` tries to write
# or delete files the operating system owns, and "System Volume Information"
# in particular is locked down on Windows.

# --- written by the board itself ---
# saved admin settings
config.json
# CircuitPython version banner, rewritten on every boot
boot_out.txt
# may hold wifi credentials
settings.toml
# mount point for an SD card, if one is fitted
sd/

# --- macOS ---
.DS_Store
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
.fseventsd/
.TemporaryItems
.apdisk
.metadata_never_index
.documentrevisions-v100
.VolumeIcon.icns

# --- Windows ---
System Volume Information/
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/

# --- Linux ---
.Trash-*
.directory

# --- local development ---
__pycache__/
*.pyc
